1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
In the last few videos we did all

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,480
sorts of things to a mixture at equilibrium.

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,360
We added a reactant, took out a product,

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,760
squeezed the container.

5
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,240
The mixture shifted every time, but K never

6
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:12,800
moved.

7
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,079
Here is a sealed tube of nitrogen dioxide,

8
00:00:16,121 --> 00:00:18,880
the brown gas, in balance with colourless N

9
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,240
two O four.

10
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,280
In hot water it goes darker.

11
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,480
In ice it fades.

12
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:28,080
K is built from the settled concentrations, so

13
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,400
if the hot tube settles with very different

14
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:34,000
concentrations, can K really stay fixed?

15
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,480
The question is: does K change when the

16
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,640
temperature does, and which way?

17
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:42,826
First, why did K stay fixed?

18
00:00:43,147 --> 00:00:46,106
Adding a chemical or squeezing the container changes

19
00:00:46,187 --> 00:00:49,066
the amounts, so particles meet more or less

20
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:51,866
often, and for a while one reaction runs

21
00:00:51,947 --> 00:00:52,986
faster than the other.

22
00:00:53,627 --> 00:00:56,746
The mixture shifts until products over reactants is

23
00:00:56,827 --> 00:00:59,306
the same number again, even though the amounts

24
00:00:59,347 --> 00:01:00,106
are now different.

25
00:01:00,747 --> 00:01:02,826
Each collision is just as likely to work

26
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:05,146
as before, so the mixture settles at the

27
00:01:05,227 --> 00:01:06,306
same K.

28
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:10,026
Temperature is different: heating makes collisions more likely

29
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,946
to work, even with the same amounts in

30
00:01:12,027 --> 00:01:14,746
the tube, and that moves K itself.

31
00:01:15,967 --> 00:01:16,766
Here is how.

32
00:01:17,247 --> 00:01:20,926
Heating speeds up both reactions, but not equally.

33
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:23,326
As with the cobalt tube, the reaction that

34
00:01:23,407 --> 00:01:26,446
takes in heat needs harder collisions, so it

35
00:01:26,554 --> 00:01:27,806
gains the most.

36
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:30,606
Going forward, N two O four splitting takes

37
00:01:30,687 --> 00:01:33,486
in heat, so splitting speeds up far more

38
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:34,686
than joining.

39
00:01:34,767 --> 00:01:36,606
N O two builds up and N two

40
00:01:36,687 --> 00:01:39,726
O four is used up, so splitting slows

41
00:01:39,847 --> 00:01:42,286
and joining speeds up, until the rates are

42
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:44,446
equal again with more N O two and

43
00:01:44,527 --> 00:01:46,606
less N two O four than before.

44
00:01:46,847 --> 00:01:50,126
More product on top, less reactant underneath, so

45
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:51,446
K is bigger.

46
00:01:51,727 --> 00:01:54,526
A catalyst is different: it speeds up both

47
00:01:54,607 --> 00:01:57,326
reactions by the same factor, so the rates

48
00:01:57,407 --> 00:02:00,446
stay equal, nothing shifts, and K stays the

49
00:02:00,527 --> 00:02:01,086
same.

50
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,620
Now the evidence.

51
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,380
The measured values for this reaction give K

52
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:11,300
as 0.0061 at twenty-five degrees Celsius,

53
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,420
and about 0.49 at a hundred degrees, about

54
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,060
eighty times bigger.

55
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:21,340
Now fill a tube with 0.040 moles per

56
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,420
litre of N two O four.

57
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,380
At twenty-five degrees only about eighteen percent of

58
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:29,260
it splits, so the tube is pale.

59
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:32,220
At a hundred degrees about seventy-nine percent has

60
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:35,100
split, so it is a deep brown.

61
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,500
A bigger K is what that deeper brown

62
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:38,220
looks like.

63
00:02:39,434 --> 00:02:42,713
Now write the same reaction backwards: two N

64
00:02:42,834 --> 00:02:45,633
O two making N two O four.

65
00:02:45,914 --> 00:02:48,713
Going this way the reaction gives out heat,

66
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:50,713
the same amount that the other way takes

67
00:02:50,794 --> 00:02:51,313
in.

68
00:02:51,594 --> 00:02:53,433
Its K is the flip of the old

69
00:02:53,514 --> 00:02:54,153
one.

70
00:02:54,234 --> 00:02:59,033
One over 0.0061 is about 160 at twenty-five

71
00:02:59,114 --> 00:03:03,593
degrees, and one over 0.49 is about 2.0

72
00:03:03,754 --> 00:03:04,953
at a hundred.

73
00:03:05,034 --> 00:03:07,433
So here K falls when you heat it.

74
00:03:08,634 --> 00:03:09,113
Why?

75
00:03:09,514 --> 00:03:12,233
It is the same tube going brown; only

76
00:03:12,274 --> 00:03:14,193
the way we write it has changed.

77
00:03:14,474 --> 00:03:16,793
Heating speeds up the reaction that takes in

78
00:03:16,874 --> 00:03:19,513
heat more, and written this way that is

79
00:03:19,554 --> 00:03:22,873
the reverse reaction, N two O four splitting.

80
00:03:22,954 --> 00:03:25,113
So N two O four, which is now

81
00:03:25,154 --> 00:03:27,993
the product, gets used up, and the settled

82
00:03:28,127 --> 00:03:29,673
mixture holds less product.

83
00:03:30,074 --> 00:03:31,473
K is smaller.

84
00:03:31,834 --> 00:03:32,793
So here is the rule.

85
00:03:33,274 --> 00:03:36,313
If the forward reaction takes in heat, heating

86
00:03:36,394 --> 00:03:37,473
raises K.

87
00:03:37,754 --> 00:03:40,633
If the forward reaction gives out heat, heating

88
00:03:40,714 --> 00:03:41,913
lowers K.

89
00:03:42,034 --> 00:03:43,433
Cooling does the opposite.

90
00:03:44,634 --> 00:03:46,873
Let's put the four changes side by side

91
00:03:46,954 --> 00:03:47,673
in a table.

92
00:03:48,154 --> 00:03:50,953
The first three, adding N two O four,

93
00:03:51,034 --> 00:03:53,833
squeezing the container and adding a catalyst, leave

94
00:03:53,914 --> 00:03:54,793
K alone.

95
00:03:55,354 --> 00:03:57,673
Heat the tube, and the two reactions speed

96
00:03:57,754 --> 00:04:00,233
up by different amounts, so K changes.

97
00:04:00,874 --> 00:04:02,633
A shift is Q moving.

98
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,353
A change in K is the target itself

99
00:04:05,434 --> 00:04:06,113
moving.

100
00:04:06,394 --> 00:04:08,393
Only temperature moves the target.

101
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,600
Link it to the reaction quotient video.

102
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:15,040
Take the tube settled at twenty-five degrees, with

103
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:18,640
0.0329 moles per litre of N two O

104
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:22,920
four and 0.0142 of N O two.

105
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:29,360
Q is 0.0142 squared over 0.0329,

106
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:33,120
which is 0.0061, equal to K.

107
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,880
Now drop it in boiling water.

108
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:38,400
The amounts have not had time to change,

109
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:42,960
so Q is still 0.0061, but K is

110
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:45,200
now 0.49.

111
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,040
Q is below K.

112
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:50,906
Q below K means that, compared with a

113
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:53,786
tube settled at a hundred degrees, this tube

114
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:56,666
holds too little N O two, so N

115
00:04:56,747 --> 00:04:58,826
two O four now splits faster than it

116
00:04:58,907 --> 00:04:59,946
forms.

117
00:05:00,027 --> 00:05:02,426
N O two builds up, and Q climbs

118
00:05:02,507 --> 00:05:04,666
until it reaches the new K.

119
00:05:04,747 --> 00:05:07,866
So heating works in two steps: first K

120
00:05:08,147 --> 00:05:10,746
changes, then the mixture moves to match it.

121
00:05:11,967 --> 00:05:13,366
Here are two lines.

122
00:05:13,567 --> 00:05:16,526
First: change T, change K.

123
00:05:17,007 --> 00:05:19,326
Change anything else, K stays.

124
00:05:19,887 --> 00:05:22,846
Second, to find the direction, treat heat like

125
00:05:22,927 --> 00:05:25,326
a chemical on one side of the equation,

126
00:05:25,447 --> 00:05:27,046
but only for the direction.

127
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,646
If the reaction takes in heat, heat is

128
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:32,206
on the left, so heating pushes the mixture

129
00:05:32,287 --> 00:05:33,806
right and K goes up.

130
00:05:34,287 --> 00:05:36,046
If it gives out heat, heat is on

131
00:05:36,087 --> 00:05:38,326
the right, so K goes down.

132
00:05:38,607 --> 00:05:41,166
Unlike a real reactant, heat speeds the two

133
00:05:41,247 --> 00:05:43,966
reactions up by different amounts, which is why

134
00:05:44,047 --> 00:05:45,086
K moves.

135
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:46,940
Your turn.

136
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,940
Hydrogen and iodine make hydrogen iodide in a

137
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:54,460
sealed tube, H two plus I two making

138
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:55,940
two H I.

139
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:59,100
The forward reaction gives out about 10 kilojoules

140
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:01,100
for each mole of hydrogen used.

141
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:06,020
At about 450 degrees Celsius, K is 49.

142
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:08,780
The tube is heated to 500 degrees and

143
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,740
left to settle.

144
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:13,900
Is K now above 49, equal to 49,

145
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,180
or below 49?

146
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,980
Give a short reason.

147
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:18,540
Pause here to answer.

148
00:06:28,967 --> 00:06:31,966
The forward reaction gives out heat, so the

149
00:06:32,007 --> 00:06:34,406
reverse reaction is the one that takes in

150
00:06:34,567 --> 00:06:35,046
heat.

151
00:06:35,367 --> 00:06:38,006
Heating speeds up the reverse reaction more than

152
00:06:38,047 --> 00:06:40,806
the forward one, so the settled tube ends

153
00:06:40,887 --> 00:06:43,606
with a little less hydrogen iodide, and K

154
00:06:43,687 --> 00:06:46,646
falls: it is below 49.

155
00:06:46,687 --> 00:06:49,126
It falls only slightly, because the heat involved

156
00:06:49,207 --> 00:06:50,406
is small.

157
00:06:50,447 --> 00:06:52,406
The N two O four reaction takes in

158
00:06:52,487 --> 00:06:54,886
much more heat, and its K grew about

159
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:56,566
eighty times.

160
00:06:56,647 --> 00:06:58,966
If you said K rises because everything is

161
00:06:59,047 --> 00:07:01,926
faster, remember that both speed up, and it

162
00:07:02,007 --> 00:07:05,046
is which one speeds up more that decides.

163
00:07:05,087 --> 00:07:07,606
If you said equal, remember that K stays

164
00:07:07,687 --> 00:07:10,326
fixed only while the temperature stays fixed.

165
00:07:11,534 --> 00:07:13,373
Now the first line of the aid, as

166
00:07:13,414 --> 00:07:14,533
an extra check.

167
00:07:14,814 --> 00:07:17,773
Back at about 450 degrees, if we added

168
00:07:17,934 --> 00:07:21,773
more hydrogen instead, K would stay at 49,

169
00:07:21,854 --> 00:07:24,813
because adding hydrogen changes the amounts, not the

170
00:07:24,894 --> 00:07:25,693
temperature.

171
00:07:25,934 --> 00:07:29,053
What changes is Q: more hydrogen in the

172
00:07:29,254 --> 00:07:32,733
reactants makes Q smaller, so Q falls below

173
00:07:32,894 --> 00:07:35,453
K, and the mixture shifts right to use

174
00:07:35,534 --> 00:07:36,813
some of the extra hydrogen.

175
00:07:37,294 --> 00:07:39,453
If you think K changed because the mixture

176
00:07:39,534 --> 00:07:43,133
shifted, separate the two: a shift means Q

177
00:07:43,214 --> 00:07:44,653
moved toward K.

178
00:07:45,134 --> 00:07:47,133
K itself did not move.

179
00:07:48,334 --> 00:07:51,613
So when a question changes the temperature, ask:

180
00:07:52,014 --> 00:07:54,413
does the forward reaction take in heat or

181
00:07:54,494 --> 00:07:55,133
give it out?

182
00:07:55,694 --> 00:07:57,613
Then use the rule you just saw.

183
00:07:58,174 --> 00:08:00,413
You can run the rule backwards too: if

184
00:08:00,494 --> 00:08:03,053
a table shows K rising as the temperature

185
00:08:03,134 --> 00:08:06,613
rises, the forward reaction takes in heat.

186
00:08:07,054 --> 00:08:09,453
Next: how a colour reading can give you

187
00:08:09,494 --> 00:08:10,573
a real K.

188
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,240
Here are the key notes.

189
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,400
Pause the video if you need more time

190
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,280
to copy them.
